# FastAPI conventions

- Async everywhere (`async def`). No blocking calls in a request handler.
- `POST /jobs` (and any other work-creating POST) requires an `Idempotency-Key` header.
  Reject with 400 if absent; look up the key in Redis before doing any work.
- Long-running work never blocks the request. Return `202 Accepted` + `job_id` immediately;
  the pipeline runs via the graph, progress is polled or streamed from Redis.
- Error responses use one stable envelope: `{ "code": ..., "message": ..., "trace_id": ... }`.
  Every error, including 4xx, carries a `trace_id` so a support request can open the exact
  Langfuse trace.
- Request/response bodies are Pydantic models only — no raw dict passthrough at the route
  boundary.
